      "problem": "What is the distance between the points $(-9,2)$ and $(-12,-4)?$",
      "worked_solution": "In this case, we have ${{(-9,2)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and ${{(-12,-4)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})}.$\nSo, the distance $d$ can be calculated using the distance formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})^{2}+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-12-(-9))^{2}+(-4-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{45} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
